      "body": "Records the dated OCapN/CapTP watch entry that issue #6014 asks for, and the trigger test that decides when the CapTP bridge spike is worth running. Docs only — no implementation.\n\n## What this changes\n\n- Adds `doc/2026-11-08T13-20-00Z_research_id6014_ocapn_captp_watch/`, a standing watch record with:\n  - the **2026-11-08 dated entry** (first entry, evidence gathered fresh today);\n  - the **trigger test (T1–T3)** that replaces \"run the spike someday\" with a decidable condition;\n  - the **cadence**: the re-check folds into the worlds-programme research pass on #5989, per the 2026-11-05 triage scoping note;\n  - the shape a future entry must have, so an unchanged watch costs one line.\n\n## The 2026-11-08 verdict: deferral stands, spike not triggered\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| T1 — docs drop the \"not stable\" caution | **Fails.** `.../guile-goblins/latest/OCapN.html` still says *\"CAUTION: CapTP support is still in its early days. Please do not rely on the protocol being stable at this time.\"* |\n| T2 — a published OCapN version stops breaking | **Fails.** Goblins 0.18.0 (2026-04-21): *\"The OCapN draft specification has changed… The protocol version number has thus been bumped, which means that applications built with an earlier release of Goblins are incompatible.\"* |\n| T3 — id needs cross-server object references | **Not met.** No worlds-programme issue requires it; worlds stay single-server, joined by capability. |\n\nSupporting: `ocapn/ocapn` has **no tags and no releases** (GitHub API, 2026-11-08); its latest commits (2026-10-13) are still protocol-shape work (`op:listen`/listen-mode, removal of `op:get`/`op:index`/`op:untag`). Spritely's 2026-10-15 E2EE-relay post adds a Noise netlayer and says a spec for the OCapN group is being written now.\n\nThis does not re-decide the position recorded in `doc/2026-10-09T09-59-07Z_design_attenuated_capabilities/` — it supplies the dated evidence that issue #6014 asks the watch to keep, and the trigger that the same record already says the deferral is revisited on.\n\n## Why the cadence is folded into #5989\n\nA standalone queue task per re-check would return to the queue every cycle with nothing landed, which is the churn that put #6014 back in the queue after triage task 10380. The watch record lives in the repo; the cadence lives with the worlds-programme research pass.\n\nCloses #6014\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796736269&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7700&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7700&signature=3cf17b6e8cfcca6ac8367f87d321eb62047f6489cf8cc51c7984cca7a743ea8a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7700?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
