      "body": "Closes #6015\n\nLands the land/parcel capability-domain design note at `doc/2026-11-08_design_id6015.md`, in the shape task 12438's re-triage and the task 12881 packet fixed:\n\n- **Parcel domain model** — a parcel is a capability domain inside a world: derived writer-set identity, author-defined extent, policy bundle (script permissions, access/ban, asset rules), control via the writer set.\n- **Nesting/attenuation rule** — effective authority is the intersection of world ceiling, enclosing parcel policies, and the actor's grant chain; every layer only narrows, widening layers are void at verification, exclusions dominate at every level.\n- **Grant shape** — control is membership in the parcel's writer set on the landed #5545 substrate (`pkgs/id/src/idset.rs`: entries admit, excludes win, `Rescind` revokes); use rights are attenuated capabilities; delegation defaults to no.\n- **Server vs author split** — inside #5975's self-hosting frame: the server enforces the invariants (monotonicity, verification, access enforcement, journaling); parcel existence, layout, and policy content are author policy and never interop requirements.\n- Cites #5989's capability-systems prior art and #5975's frame instead of re-deriving them; open points carry assumed defaults (§7). Tokenized land stays ruled out per the issue body (§6).\n\nDocs-only change; no code or tests affected.\n",
